# Verification Result Template

Use when a concrete acceptance result needs a durable record. This unfilled template is not evidence that checks ran or criteria passed.

## Candidate and scope

Identify the actual revision/candidate and relevant working-tree state, approved goal, and acceptance criteria. Do not apply evidence from a different candidate without explaining why it remains valid.

## Evidence

| Criterion | Check/source, cwd, prerequisites | Actual action/environment | Status | Evidence and limits |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |

Use passed, failed, not run, or blocked based on observations. Assess behavior against the criterion rather than exit code alone. For non-code work use the relevant review, scenario, consistency, or playtest evidence.

## Acceptance gaps

State required criteria still unproven, pre-existing failures where established, and the smallest check needed to resolve each material gap. Protect sensitive evidence with safe references/redacted summaries.

## Result and next action

Record supported acceptance or its remaining limits. Include material recovery/compatibility risks where relevant. Do not equate a clean tree, a build, or an untested backup with readiness. Acceptance does not itself authorize publication or other external action.
